],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Tyrolean speck is a distinctively juniper-flavored ham originally from Tyrol, a historical Austrian region that since 1918 partially lies in Italy. Its origins at the intersection of two culinary worlds are reflected in its synthesis of salt-curing and smoking."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-tyrolean-speck"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrolean_speck"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"]]],["Irish cuisine","cuisine/irish-cuisine",[["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Blood as food","ingredient/blood-as-food"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Suet","ingredient/suet"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/66/Fresh_speck.jpg/500px-Fresh_speck.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Hagen + Tine Graf","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fresh_speck.jpg"}},"dish/brent-s-deli":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/brent-s-deli","n":"Brent's Deli","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Jewish cuisine","dot":"#a99fb5","intro":[["Brent's Delicatessen & Restaurant is a Jewish deli and restaurant located in Northridge, California. The restaurant was opened in 1967 and purchased by Ron Peskin in 1969 for $1700. The deli has expanded to a second location in Westlake Village, California."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-brent-s-deli"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brent's_Deli"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Tori Avey: Jewish Recipes","ref":"site/toriavey-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape"