red. It is made of wheat flour with yeast or sourdough starter. It is shaped into oval or round loaves with longitudinal or criss-crossed scoring. The characteristic golden or golden-brown color of its crust is achieved by coating the surface of the loaves with sweetened tea essence before baking."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-matnakash"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matnakash"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Armenian cuisine","cuisine/armenian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Sourdough starter","ingredient/sourdough-starter"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Armenian Kitchen","ref":"site/thearmeniankitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thearmeniankitchen.com","note":"Armenian-American blog of family recipes and reviews of Armenian cookbooks.","url":"https://www.thearmeniankitchen.com/classic-armenian-recipes-another/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Armenian cuisine","links":[["Alani (dried fruit)","dish/alani-dried-fruit"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bagharj","dish/bagharj"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Khorovats","dish/khorovats"],["Lavash","dish/lavash"],["Mikado cake","dish/mikado-cake"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Spas (soup)","dish/spas-soup"],["Tjvjik (food)","dish/tjvjik-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a8/Matnakash.JPG/500px-Matnakash.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Narek75","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matnakash.JPG"}},"dish/roti":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/roti","n":"Roti","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Bengali cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Roti is a round flatbread originating from the Indian subcontinent. It is comm